 Two-Client Convergence (via ot.ts transformOperation)\n- [ ] Edits at different (disjoint) positions converge correctly regardless of order.\n- [ ] Concurrent inserts at the same position: both preserved, none dropped.\n- [ ] Insert + delete concurrently: both effects present.\n- [ ] Rapid alternating edits from 2 clients: all chars present, no corruption.\n- [ ] All clients converge to identical content for the same doc.\n- [ ] Version history records every operation, strictly increasing version numbers.\n- [ ] Concurrent edits without explicit ordering never lose data (server serializes + transforms).\n- [ ] Edits at opposite ends concurrently both land correctly.\n\n## Stress (10 concurrent clients)\n- [ ] 10 clients can connect simultaneously to one doc.\n- [ ] 10 clients each send an edit — all 10 edits present in the final doc.\n- [ ] After settling, all 10 clients see identical content on reconnect/sync.\n- [ ] 50 rapid-fire edits from one client — no crash, all applied (length 50).\n- [ ] All 10 clients can disconnect at once without server error; server stays healthy.\n\n## Error Handling\n- [ ] Connecting to a non-existent doc id sends `{type:'error', message: '...not found...'}`.\n- [ ] Malformed JSON over the socket → `{type:'error'}`, connection stays open.\n- [ ] Unknown operation type (e.g. `replace`) → `{type:'error'}`.\n- [ ] Out-of-bounds operation (e.g. delete past end) → `{type:'error'}`.\n- [ ] Server remains stable and usable (REST + WS) after bad input.\n\n## Persistence (SQLite via better-sqlite3, schema.sql)\n- [ ] Documents survive server restart (same dbPath reopened).\n- [ ] Version/edit history survives restart.\n- [ ] `active_connections` table is cleared on startup (stale rows from a previous run don't linger).\n\n## Verification commands\n```bash\nnpm run build\nnpm run lint\nnpm test\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tok