+# Contract: Real-Time Markdown Collab Server
+
+## Build / Lint
+- [x] `npm run build` — TypeScript compiles with no errors.
+- [x] `npm run lint` — ESLint passes with no errors.
+
+## REST CRUD (tests/collab.test.ts "REST CRUD")
+- [x] POST /docs creates a document, returns 201 + `{title}`.
+- [x] POST /docs response has id, title, content, created_at, updated_at.
+- [x] GET /docs returns array of all documents, 200.
+- [x] GET /docs/:id returns the document, 200.
+- [x] GET /docs/:id returns 404 for unknown id.
+- [x] PUT /docs/:id updates title, returns updated doc, 200.
+- [x] DELETE /docs/:id removes doc, 204, subsequent GET is 404.
+- [x] DELETE /docs/:id returns 404 for unknown id.
+- [x] GET /docs/:id/versions lists version history, first entry version 0.
+- [x] GET /docs/:id/versions/:version returns `{content, version}` for that version.
+
+## WebSocket Lifecycle
+- [x] Client connects to `ws://host:port/:docId`.
+- [x] On connect, server sends `{type:'sync', content, version}` first.
+- [x] Sending `{type:'operation', operation}` returns `{type:'ack', version}`.
+- [x] Other clients in the same doc room receive `{type:'operation', operation}` broadcast.
+- [x] The sender does NOT receive its own op echoed back as a broadcast (only ack).
+- [x] Client can disconnect cleanly (readyState CLOSED).
+- [x] Multiple clients (3+) can join the same doc concurrently.
+- [x] Clients on different docs are isolated — no cross-doc leakage.
+
+## Single Client Editing (via ot.ts applyOperation)
+- [x] Insert at beginning / middle / end works correctly.
+- [x] Delete range works correctly.
+- [x] Sequential edits build up content correctly in order.
+- [x] Version increments by 1 per accepted edit.
+
+## Two-Client Convergence (via ot.ts transformOperation)
+- [x] Edits at different (disjoint) positions converge correctly regardless of order.
+- [x] Concurrent inserts at the same position: both preserved, none dropped.
+- [x] Insert + delete concurrently: both effects present.
+- [x] Rapid alternating edits from 2 clients: all chars present, no corruption.
+- [x] All clients converge to identical content for the same doc.
+- [x] Version history records every operation, strictly increasing version numbers.
+- [x] Concurrent edits without explicit ordering never lose data (server serializes + transforms).
+- [x] Edits at opposite ends concurrently both land correctly.
+
+## Stress (10 concurrent clients)
+- [x] 10 clients can connect simultaneously to one doc.
+- [x] 10 clients each send an edit — all 10 edits present in the final doc.
+- [x] After settling, all 10 clients see identical content on reconnect/sync.
+- [x] 50 rapid-fire edits from one client — no crash, all applied (length 50).
+- [x] All 10 clients can disconnect at once without server error; server stays healthy.
+
+## Error Handling
+- [x] Connecting to a non-existent doc id sends `{type:'error', message: '...not found...'}`.
+- [x] Malformed JSON over the socket → `{type:'error'}`, connection stays open.
+- [x] Unknown operation type (e.g. `replace`) → `{type:'error'}`.
+- [x] Out-of-bounds operation (e.g. delete past end) → `{type:'error'}`.
+- [x] Server remains stable and usable (REST + WS) after bad input.
+
+## Persistence (SQLite via better-sqlite3, schema.sql)
+- [x] Documents survive server restart (same dbPath reopened).
+- [x] Version/edit history survives restart.
+- [x] `active_connections` table is cleared on startup (stale rows from a previous run don't linger).
+
+## Verification commands
+```bash
+npm run build
+npm run lint
+npm test
+```
